# A nightly report template belonging to a different project (it names the repo
# robinbakshi007/ollama-direct-custom-agent and counts VS Code marketplace
# releases). Nothing here generates it; ignored so an external writer cannot
# reintroduce it as tracked noise.
JULES_REPORT.md

.vercel
_worktrees/

.vercel

.vercel
.env*

.vercel
.env*
# The template stays tracked; every other .env* (.env, .env.docker, ...) is private.
!.env.example

apps/server/src/generated/

# Written by apps/server/scripts/doc-graph.mjs on every regeneration, and read
# by nothing: the file's own note says it is "excluded from every
# staleness/consistency check by design", and a search for its path finds one
# writer and no reader. PR #278 introduced it to hold the drift diff that used
# to be baked into docs/.doc-graph.json, where it went stale against itself and
# failed `monorepo-graph.mjs --check` on fresh checkouts — the right fix, but
# tracked it carried a `generated_at` timestamp, so it conflicted on the very
# first merge after landing and would have on every one after. Untracked, the
# diagnostic still gets written and printed; only the merge churn goes away.
docs/.doc-graph-drift-report.json

# Generated documentation views (ADR-081). Written by `npm run govern`, verified
# in CI, never committed. The drift report above was the first file to earn this
# treatment for exactly this reason; these are the rest of the same family.
#
# On 2026-09-12 six pull requests merged and the generated files accounted for
# 11 of 15 conflicts on two of them, 2 of 2 on a three-file CI change, and 5 of 5
# on a fourth. None was a disagreement about anything a person wrote — two
# branches ran one generator over different inputs and git was asked to referee.
#
# NOT listed, and deliberately still committed: `apps/server/runtime/domain-state.json`
# (imported by `product-readiness-read-model.js`, and the Docker build context is
# `apps/server/`, so the repo-root `docs/` it derives from is absent at image
# build time), `llms-full.txt` and `llms.txt` (their purpose is to be readable
# without a checkout). See ADR-081 D2 — a file joins that list only with a
# reason of that kind.
docs/.doc-graph.json
docs/.domain-state.json
docs/.preflight-report.json
docs/FEATURE-MAP.md
docs/DOMAIN-MAP.md
docs/TRACE.md
docs/DOCUMENT-LINKS.md
docs/appendices/D-traceability.md

# `llms-full.txt` joins them. It was argued for keeping — its purpose is to be
# readable without a checkout — and the merge ledger overruled that: it
# conflicted on four of the five pull requests merged on 2026-09-12, more often
# than any other single file, because it inlines README, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md,
# PRODUCT.md and every charter, so any edit to any of them rewrites it whole.
# CI builds it and uploads it as an artefact, which serves a reader without a
# checkout at least as well as a file that is regularly wrong between merges.
llms-full.txt

.claude/worktrees/
